# SFT execution status v0.128: native failure localized to coordinator call

2026-09-28 Asia/Dhaka (2026-09-27 UTC). The approved v2 diagnostic successor
ran exactly once. It failed with **stage_coordinate_import**, child/worker
exit status **47**. This is useful localization, not a successful import or
an established internal root cause. Gate 5 remains incomplete. No real S3
model/checkpoint/dataset, GPU, inference, training or production approval.

## Execution and observed boundaries

The same fresh t3.large created before the user interruption was resumed;
no replacement instance or repeated native attempt was launched. The VM was
created at 18:28:42 UTC and confirmed terminated before 18:47:14 UTC, within
the 60-minute lifetime. An initial local CLI count-option rejection occurred
before the launch API request; correcting it did not start a second instance.

All ten prepared artifact bindings matched. Boot health, pinned SSH host key,
expiry timer, cgroup controllers, worker identity, no IAM profile, mandatory
IMDS token and encrypted 20-GiB delete-on-termination storage were verified.
Staging installed the 34 hash-pinned CPU wheels (248,715,637 bytes) under the
non-resetting HTTPS quota. Quota accounting ended at 290,518,141 bytes, below
1 GiB, with no quota drops. Actual billed cost was not queried or asserted.

Preparation completed: the supervisor advanced to import, and the independent
bounded system journal showed successful deactivation. The independent polling
observer missed its transient terminal snapshot; its terminal field is null,
not fabricated as an observed exit zero. It sampled 255 preparation cgroup
observations with a maximum of 284,475,392 bytes. These are sampled values,
not exhaustive memory peaks.

For import, the independent observer captured status 47 / exit-code / failed
and six cgroup observations, sampled maximum 21,176,320 bytes. The root
failure record retained `stage_coordinate_import`, retry_allowed=false.
Bound-source inspection maps 47 to the coordinator call after the entry's
cold loader, initial runtime gate, read-only inputs, writable output and
control-read/contract checks. It does not prove the coordinator's repeated
runtime gate, source preflight, path checks or conversion succeeded.

Both exact cgroups were absent after failure; the stage directory was empty
and unmounted, no cleanup-failure record existed, and all 49 original staged
source hashes still matched. No failed attempt was retried or modified.

